# Plan (opus, strong)

## Goal

When the opponent replies to a line, it also tries its `Activate` (and `ActivatePower`) actions whose source the seat can see. The source must be face-up on the field and none of the cards the opponent held unseen. A face-down card's Reveal, including one determinization filled in, is never used. Each activation is scored like a known play by the opponent's own evaluation: a winning one is taken at once, otherwise the best is used only when it beats standing still.

- A new cap, `AI_REPLY.visible_activations` (4), bounds the tries per step. It is separate from `known_plays`, so activations never crowd out known plays.
- The tries are sorted so that those aimed at the seat's hero come first. A lethal one is therefore never past the cap.
- SPEC §9.9, `docs/polish/3-ai.md` (the reply surface and B41) and `crates/ai/README.md` say this.
- `GREEDY_EVAL`, the greedy baseline and the existing reply tests stay unchanged. No ruling is added, because this is an AI heuristic and not a rules decision.

